  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Approach on Older Persons in Qudra 2 Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective 1 (upstream): Strengthen the capacity of partners&apos; staff and the programmatic frameworks and tools on inclusion of older people</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective 2 (downstream): Support the implementation of activities that address the specific needs of older people through provision of technical support, monitoring and feedback</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Qudra 2 project is oriented towards the &#x201C;Leave No One Behind&#x201D; principle with special considerations to disadvantaged population groups. HAI will provide its technical assistance to capacitate and empower Qudra 2 partners so that they are able to include effectively older people, including those with disabilities, in Qudra 2 planned interventions and to design tailor-made interventions for this category of population with specific needs. 
Through this project, HAI will be able to develop the capacity of at least 60 staff of NGO partners , SDCs, and the Ministry of Social Affairs (MoSA) in addition to approximately 160 community volunteers mobilised by SDCs and NGO partners to identify and address protection and health related issues of older people and to design age-inclusive activities ensuring the integration of older people among their communities and improved access to services.
This will be done through the establishment of a technical assistance facility for the provision of upstream and downstream guidance and support. The Inclusion Training Coordinator based in Lebanon will be the focal point for the technical assistance facility. S/he will coordinate all training activities and will technically supervise the Field Inclusion Officers, supporting them with tools, reviewing their reports and providing feedback on their activities. Monthly coordination meetings including the Inclusion Training Coordinator, all Field Inclusion Officers and the implementing SDC and NGO staff, will be organised to monitor and evaluate the progress of activities and provide  technical support as needed.HAI&apos;s global Protection Adviser and global Inclusion Adviser will provide overall technical guidance to the project. They will be directly involved in training and coaching HAI&apos;s Lebanon team at the beginning and during the course of the project, contribute to reviewing project tools and processes, and monitor the project implementation through field visits.
The frequency and intensity of the project activities are scalable depending on the allocated budget and duration of the overall project.</narrative>
  </description>
